4. Upstream wheel (local benchmarking only)

   tools/fetch.sh downloads cactus_needle-3.3.3-py3-none-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
   from the needle3 Hugging Face repository into ref/hf/wheel/. It contains
   the native library libneedle3.so. It is used only to compare speed on a
   developer machine. It must never be committed, packaged or shipped.

5. Test audio clips (downloaded, not redistributed)

   tools/fetch.sh downloads test.wav, test_long.wav, hotword.wav and
   record.wav from the cactus-compute/cactus repository into ref/audio/,
   which is git-ignored. They are not part of this repository. Check the
   license that applies to that repository before using them anywhere
   other than local testing.

